## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of event-driven orchestration, idempotency, and minimal IAM in a data enrichment flow that uses Cloud Functions, Pub/Sub, and Cloud Run.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven pipeline with Cloud Functions, Pub/Sub, Cloud Run
- Idempotent writes via insertId and dedup strategies
- Dead-letter handling and exponential backoff retries
- Least privilege IAM and secure service-to-service communication

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Cloud Function: validate and publish to Pub/Sub
const {PubSub} = require('@google-cloud/pubsub');
const pubsub = new PubSub();
exports.validateAndPublish = (req, res) => {
  const evt = req.body; // simple schema check omitted
  const data = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(evt));
  pubsub.topic('enrich-events').publish(data);
  res.status(200).send('ok');
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test handling of out-of-order message delivery?
- What changes ensure exactly-once processing when writing to BigQuery?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design real-time, multi-tenant data pipelines with correct deduplication, rate limiting, and safe cross-tenant isolation. It also probes for practical IAM scoping, dead-letter handling, and observability under burst traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub streaming ingestion, Apache Beam (Dataflow) processing
- Deduplication by tenant_id + event_id with windowing
- Per-tenant rate limiting using Redis
- External risk-score enrichment via internal API
- Multi-tenant BigQuery routing: analytics.tenants.{tenant}.events
- Dead-letter queues, exponential backoff retries
- Least-privilege IAM, monitoring, alerting, cost control

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-Beam-style dedup snippet
// Deduplicate by (tenant_id, event_id) using per-tenant state
class DedupFn {
  process(element) {
    const key = element.tenant_id + ':' + element.event_id;
    if (state.has(key)) return;
    state.add(key);
    yield element;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant rate limiting and data skew at scale?
- How would you secure Redis and ensure tenant isolation for secrets?
- How would you handle late-arriving events that would violate dedup windows?
